{"name":"Potting Soil","hex":"#5b3e31","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"potting soil","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A substrate used to grow plants in containers, made from various substances that promote moisture, drainage, and fertility."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/potting_soil"}],"entries":[{"title":"Potting soil","blocks":[{"text":"Potting soil or growing media, also known as potting mix or potting compost (UK), is a substrate used to grow plants in containers. The first recorded use of the term is from an 1861 issue of the American Agriculturist."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Potting_soil.jpg/330px-Potting_soil.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Potting_soil"},{"title":"Soil","blocks":[{"text":"Soil, also commonly referred to as earth, is a mixture of organic matter, minerals, gases, water, and organisms that together support the life of plants and soil organisms. Some scientific definitions distinguish dirt from soil by restricting the former term specifically to displaced soil."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Stagnogley.JPG/330px-Stagnogley.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soil"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/EAgronom_4okt2023_L-1120.jpg/500px-EAgronom_4okt2023_L-1120.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/EAgronom_4okt2023_L-1120.jpg/1280px-EAgronom_4okt2023_L-1120.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/EAgronom_4okt2023_L-1120.jpg/500px-EAgronom_4okt2023_L-1120.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Soil measuring and surveying device","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEAgronom_4okt2023_L-1120.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Estructura-suelo.jpg/500px-Estructura-suelo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Estructura-suelo.jpg/500px-Estructura-suelo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A, B, and C represent the soil profile, a notation firstly coined by Vasily Dokuchaev (1846–1903), the father of pedology. Here, A is the topsoil; B is a regolith; C is a saprolite (a less-weathered regolith); the bottom-most layer represents the bedrock.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEstructura-suelo.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Soil_erosion%2C_Southfield_-_geograph.org.uk_-_367917.jpg/500px-Soil_erosion%2C_Southfield_-_geograph.org.uk_-_367917.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Soil_erosion%2C_Southfield_-_geograph.org.uk_-_367917.jpg/500px-Soil_erosion%2C_Southfield_-_geograph.org.uk_-_367917.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Desertification","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASoil_erosion%2C_Southfield_-_geograph.org.uk_-_367917.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Riparian_buffer_on_Bear_Creek_in_Story_County%2C_Iowa.JPG/500px-Riparian_buffer_on_Bear_Creek_in_Story_County%2C_Iowa.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Riparian_buffer_on_Bear_Creek_in_Story_County%2C_Iowa.JPG/1280px-Riparian_buffer_on_Bear_Creek_in_Story_County%2C_Iowa.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","